record.authors_conclusion:
Mostly correct. The authors conclude that:
- the a/an phonological feature is a one-dimensional direction in token embeddings that causally drives article choice (wug tests);
- at the article position the model forecasts the upcoming trigger and uses its phonological feature to choose the article, also in a 70B model and in French and Italian;
- this generation-time feature is dissociated from explicit sound judgments.
They call the FutureLens-based mechanism a limited account that does not identify the exact circuit.
